 best option: Play 777 with the 5. I should not lead with the 5. Get that orphan out. Then let the opponents figure out what to do with their cards. I should keep the 999! This should be a good move.\n\nThus, the move is: **"♦5", "♥7", "♣7", "♦7"**\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The hand contains multiple pairs (33, 44, 66, 88) and two triples (777, 999). There is an isolated single 5. While a straight (3-4-5-6-7-8-9) is possible, playing it would disastrously break up all the pairs and the 999 triple, leaving a hand full of loose, low singles. The pairs are relatively low, so starting with a pair is weak. The most structural approach is to play "Triples with Singles". The 5 is the weakest card and should be discarded as the kicker for the lowest triple.\n\nReason: Playing the triple 777 with the single 5 clears the problematic isolated low card and the low triple immediately. This preserves the strong structural integrity of the remaining hand, which consists of four pairs, one triple, and high control cards (J, Q, K, A, 2), offering a balanced path to victory.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦5", "♥7", "♣7", "♦7"]}'}
